<title>USA: Iroquois Bancorp Inc Q3 shr $0.08 vs $0.44.</title>
<headline>Iroquois Bancorp Inc Q3 shr $0.08 vs $0.44.</headline>
<dateline>AUBURN, N.Y. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>IROQUOIS BANCORP, INC.</p>
<p>				 COMPARATIVE RESULTS</p>
<p>		   (dollars in thousands, except per share)</p>
<p>					Quarter Ended    Year Ended</p>
<p>					September 30    September 30</p>
<p>				   1996     1995	1996	1995</p>
<p> Net Interest Income	5,070    4,464     14,388    13,525</p>
<p> Provision for Loan Loss    227	204	  969	 670</p>
<p> Non-interest Income	  730	642	2,007     1,849</p>
<p>Non-interest Expense</p>
<p>  (excluding SAIF)	  3,495    3,031	9,829     9,411</p>
<p> SAIF Assessment		556	 --	  556	  --</p>
<p> Net Income		     290    1,135	2,433     3,179</p>
<p> Income per Common Share    .08	.44	  .90	1.23</p>
<p>Common Shares Outstanding:</p>
<p> Average	     2,328,716  2,322,202  2,321,942  2,303,814</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q3 results include a net of tax loss of $630,000 resulting from a writedown by Cayuga of certain classified commercial mortgage loans. Earnings for the quarter also include a one-time SAIF charge of $556,000.</p>
